Parmesan","ingredient/parmesan"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/6/64/Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Parmesan.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Parmesan.jpg","w":500,"h":332,"by":"cyclonebill","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flickr_-_cyclonebill_-_Parmesan.jpg"}},"dish/polbo-a-feira":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/polbo-a-feira","n":"Polbo á feira","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Galician cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Polbo á feira (literally meaning \"fair-style octopus\", or pulpo a la gallega in Spanish, meaning \"Galician-style octopus\"), is a traditional Galician dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-polbo-a-feira"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polbo_%C3%A1_feira"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Galician cuisine","cuisine/galician-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Common octopus","ingredient/common-octopus"],["Octopus as food","ingredient/octopus-as-food"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Paprika","ingredient/paprika"]]},{"h":"More from Galician cuisine","links":[["Androlla","dish/androlla"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Lacón","dish/lacon"],["Tarta de Santiago","dish/tarta-de-santiago"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/bf/Festa_da_Istoria_2011_%286089203513%29.jpg/500px-Festa_da_Istoria_2011_%286089203513%29.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"José Antonio Gil Martínez from Vigo, Spain","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Festa_da_Istoria_2011_(6089203513).jpg"}}}